refuse/float-literal.nz  Gate 2 added floating point (docs/internal/general-purpose.md section 1); docs/user/stability.md makes adding a construct 1.0 refused by name a 1.x minor addition, since no valid program changes meaning
refuse/array-of-strings.nz  R1a (L8) admits strings as array elements (docs/user/spec.md, Arrays and Constant tables and exported constants); a refusal lifted is a 1.x minor addition, since no valid program changes meaning
refuse/public-constant.nz  R1a (L8) exports a constant through its module's interface (docs/user/spec.md, Constant tables and exported constants); a refusal lifted is a 1.x minor addition
refuse/capture-let-mut.nz  R1b (L10) shares a captured `let mut` binding with the closure through a cell (docs/user/spec.md, Function values and closures); a refusal lifted is a 1.x minor addition, since no valid program changes meaning
refuse/question-on-option.nz  R1 (5b.17) gives `?` to an `Option` in a function that returns an `Option` (docs/user/spec.md, Errors); a refusal lifted is a 1.x minor addition, since no valid program changes meaning
refuse/missing-capability.nz  R1.5 (D8) gives the program's own functions the output authority `main` holds (docs/user/spec.md, Shorter forms), so printing there needs nothing passed; a refusal lifted is a 1.x minor addition, since no valid program changes meaning
refuse/no-ambient-authority.nz  R1.5 (D8): a function of the program's own modules holds the output authority `main` holds (docs/user/spec.md, Shorter forms); every other authority is still passed, and a package's function still holds only what it is given; a refusal lifted is a 1.x minor addition
